        "### 3. Report Format (500-600 words per stock)\n"
        "**Stock**: [Code] | [Name] | [Industry]\n"
        "1) Market Snapshot: Summarize recent OHLCV patterns — short-term trend, volatility, volume surges, breakout/decline tendencies.\n"
        "2) Price & Momentum: Discuss short-term direction and investor sentiment inferred from recent data (e.g., strong recovery, range-bound behavior, or correction risk).\n"
        "3) Fundamentals Quality: Analyze the latest fundamental metrics (ROE, gross margin, net profit YoY, debt-to-asset ratio, market cap) — highlight profitability, efficiency, leverage, and growth quality.\n"
        "4) Valuation & Relative Position: Interpret market cap, and if available, PE/PB/PS logic — compare quality vs. size vs. growth to infer valuation realism.\n"
        "5) Catalysts & News: Identify 1–3 major news items (earnings, policy, strategic actions) and their expected effect on fundamentals, valuation, or sentiment.\n"
        "6) Macro & Industry Context: Briefly relate to broader market or sector trends affecting this stock’s performance (e.g., interest rate cycle, demand recovery, regulatory tone).\n"
        "7) Key Risks: Note internal (e.g., cost pressure, leverage) and external (e.g., macro slowdown, competition) risks seen in data or news.\n"
